+## Phase41 wrapper experiment
+
+Phase41 is evaluating a narrow acyclic wrapper rule around an already admitted
+recursive worker. Its checked01 tree candidate adds 35 Bend source lines: a
+leaf or nonrecursive wrapper runs once and returns the recursive worker's
+result, without allocating continuation frames. The recursive worker retains
+the existing structural frame engine. Admission requires the existing typed
+prefix and complete closed-graph proof, a nonbuiltin ADT first argument, and a
+direct reference to an independently admitted recursive worker; the planner
+does not follow chains of acyclic wrappers.
+
+Existing exact-entry and dependency guards, the generic fallback, tagged
+representation and child/result order remain in force. The experiment adds no
+runtime code and leaves the TypeScript target pinned to
+`018751270e800bc222a93dad7f257083ee53a5f7`. Checked01 tree controls and the
+execution screen pass; independent fixture controls and promotion remain
+pending, so this is not an installed compiler change. See the
+[Phase41 report](../implementation/phase41/README.md) for the evidence and the
+separate lexer and list decisions.
+
